1
00:00:01,127 --> 00:00:03,379
They've got to stop them in this series.

2
00:00:05,173 --> 00:00:06,966
Geez! - Come on! Damn it!

3
00:00:07,425 --> 00:00:16,559
In Texas, the holy Trinity is god, football and barbeque, not necessarily in that order.

4
00:00:16,893 --> 00:00:21,105
I don't care if you win, just cover the damn spread.

5
00:00:21,314 --> 00:00:22,394
Mom, are you betting again?

6
00:00:22,565 --> 00:00:23,565
No.

7
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:26,044
Fans on their feet, trying to urge the defense on.

8
00:00:26,068 --> 00:00:27,195
Fourth down.

9
00:00:27,403 --> 00:00:28,446
Gotta punt.

10
00:00:28,654 --> 00:00:29,654
Gotta.

11
00:00:29,906 --> 00:00:33,408
Statistically, always punting on fourth down makes no sense.

12
00:00:33,576 --> 00:00:35,161
Statistically, you're a dumb-ass.

13
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:35,995
Hey.

14
00:00:36,204 --> 00:00:42,960
When the aggies give up the ball on their own five-yard line, the opposing team has a 92% chance of scoring.

15
00:00:43,169 --> 00:00:48,549
When they punt from deep in their own territory, the other team still has a 77% chance of scoring.

16
00:00:48,758 --> 00:00:55,348
But since they convert on fourth down 50% of the time, the math says they should never punt again.

17
00:00:58,559 --> 00:01:01,354
Okay, you can tell me, who's his real daddy?

18
00:01:03,147 --> 00:01:06,400
Sheldon, I've been playing and coaching football all my life.

19
00:01:06,651 --> 00:01:07,985
I don't think your math is right.

20
00:01:08,486 --> 00:01:09,529
Really?

21
00:01:09,737 --> 00:01:11,030
Hang on.

22
00:01:11,864 --> 00:01:12,864
No, it's right.

23
00:01:12,949 --> 00:01:16,077
Able to hold a&m to a field goal, they'll only be down six points.

24
00:01:16,285 --> 00:01:17,453
Is it your dentist?

25
00:01:17,662 --> 00:01:19,080
The little guy with the glasses?

26
00:01:19,539 --> 00:01:20,665
You can tell me.

27
00:01:21,707 --> 00:01:24,460
♪ nobody else ♪ is stronger than I am

28
00:01:24,669 --> 00:01:27,380
♪ j" yesterday I moved a mountain

29
00:01:27,588 --> 00:01:29,924
♪ j" I bet I could be your hero

30
00:01:30,132 --> 00:01:32,760
♪ j" I am a mighty little man

31
00:01:32,969 --> 00:01:36,264
♪ j" I am a mighty little man.

32
00:01:41,602 --> 00:01:43,813
I got to tell you, I'm a little worried about my mother.

33
00:01:44,021 --> 00:01:49,735
She keeps betting on these football games, next thing you know, there's an Italian fella driving off with her pickup truck.

34
00:01:53,281 --> 00:01:54,321
You think Sheldon's right?

35
00:01:54,574 --> 00:01:55,658
About what?

36
00:01:55,866 --> 00:01:58,035
The punting and the math.

37
00:01:58,786 --> 00:01:59,912
I should think so.

38
00:02:00,121 --> 00:02:02,123
He's been doing our taxes since he's six years old.

39
00:02:02,331 --> 00:02:03,457
We never been audited.

40
00:02:04,208 --> 00:02:05,293
That's true.

41
00:02:08,462 --> 00:02:10,881
He even got us that nice refund last year.

42
00:02:11,841 --> 00:02:17,847
♪ I got some ocean front ♪ property in Arizona...

43
00:02:18,097 --> 00:02:20,474
how come mom's not taking me to school?

44
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:24,312
'Cause once in a while, your dad wants to spend some time with you.

45
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,730
My little shel-man.

46
00:02:27,523 --> 00:02:29,317
But mom's car has a backseat.

47
00:02:29,525 --> 00:02:31,068
Statistically, I'm much safer there.

48
00:02:31,277 --> 00:02:33,112
Hey, I'm glad you brought up statistically.

49
00:02:33,321 --> 00:02:37,325
You think those numbers you talked about for Texas a&m would apply to my jv squad?

50
00:02:37,658 --> 00:02:39,327
I don't see why not.

51
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:43,497
Unlike our former principal, math doesn't discriminate.

52
00:02:45,041 --> 00:02:47,121
You're not thinking about taking his advice, are you?

53
00:02:47,293 --> 00:02:49,378
Never you mind. But he's wrong.

54
00:02:49,587 --> 00:02:51,464
Everybody knows you punt on fourth down.

55
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:54,258
Why does everybody knowing something make it right?

56
00:02:54,675 --> 00:02:55,885
Because.

57
00:02:58,262 --> 00:03:00,348
That's what makes this country great.

58
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:06,020
Many years later, my brother would use this same argument in front of a judge.

59
00:03:06,228 --> 00:03:09,315
He was still convicted for urinating in a phone booth.

60
00:03:21,744 --> 00:03:23,287
Oh, damn it.

61
00:03:23,496 --> 00:03:24,696
I'll send in the punting team.

62
00:03:24,914 --> 00:03:25,914
Hang on. Hang on.

63
00:03:26,082 --> 00:03:27,082
What?

64
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:29,543
Let's go for it.

65
00:03:29,752 --> 00:03:31,587
Why? We got plenty of time.

66
00:03:31,796 --> 00:03:33,756
I know. Still want to go for it.

67
00:03:34,548 --> 00:03:37,051
We're on the 12-yard line. Everybody know you punt.

68
00:03:37,259 --> 00:03:39,470
Why does everybody knowing something make it right?

69
00:03:42,098 --> 00:03:44,475
But we're on the 12-yard line, coach.

70
00:03:46,769 --> 00:03:49,313
Okay, coach says we're going for it.

71
00:03:49,605 --> 00:03:50,898
Stupid brother.

72
00:03:51,107 --> 00:03:52,692
What? Nothing.

73
00:03:53,109 --> 00:03:55,653
Power left jumbo on two, on two. Ready? Break!

74
00:03:56,404 --> 00:03:59,156
P.A. announcer: And your wolves are going for it on fourth down.

75
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,367
What the hell? Punt!

76
00:04:01,826 --> 00:04:03,953
Statistically, they're better off going for it.

77
00:04:04,161 --> 00:04:06,497
Says who? My little boy.

78
00:04:13,838 --> 00:04:15,214
That's why everybody punts.

79
00:04:15,423 --> 00:04:17,007
That was just plain foolishness.

80
00:04:17,425 --> 00:04:19,260
Your little boy's a real genius.

81
00:04:19,468 --> 00:04:21,220
Well, actually he is.

82
00:04:24,974 --> 00:04:27,393
Too many men on the field, defense.

83
00:04:27,601 --> 00:04:28,853
Replay fourth down.

84
00:04:29,061 --> 00:04:31,605
Ah. Thank you, Jesus.

85
00:04:31,814 --> 00:04:33,774
Now, can I send in the punt team?

86
00:04:37,403 --> 00:04:38,403
Coach?

87
00:04:39,989 --> 00:04:41,073
Break!

88
00:04:43,284 --> 00:04:44,636
And they're going for it again.

89
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:46,203
What the hell? Punt!

90
00:04:46,412 --> 00:04:49,707
Remind me to tell you about the tax refund I got from the IRS.

91
00:04:50,291 --> 00:04:51,291
Set. Hut!

92
00:04:56,672 --> 00:04:58,424
Go, go, go, go, go, go!

93
00:05:00,509 --> 00:05:01,510
Go! Whoo!

94
00:05:03,012 --> 00:05:05,181
Go, go, go! Go!

95
00:05:05,389 --> 00:05:07,349
He's at the 30, the 20, the 10.

96
00:05:07,558 --> 00:05:09,769
Touchdown, wolves!

97
00:05:13,606 --> 00:05:15,816
I never had any doubt, coach. Never had any doubt.

98
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:21,113
Oh, booyah! Yes.

99
00:05:30,956 --> 00:05:32,333
Sweet dreams, baby.

100
00:05:32,541 --> 00:05:33,709
Mwah.

101
00:05:34,043 --> 00:05:35,711
Night, meemaw.

102
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:39,882
Can I ask you a favor?

103
00:05:40,341 --> 00:05:44,275
Sure. What? You know those statistics that you were talking about with your dad?

104
00:05:44,428 --> 00:05:50,559
Could... could that be applied to, say, who might win the cowboys-packers game next week?

105
00:05:50,768 --> 00:05:53,896
And, more specifically, by how much?

106
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:58,067
I suppose with enough data I could make a reasonable guess.

107
00:05:58,275 --> 00:06:00,402
I don't want a guess, I want to know.

108
00:06:00,611 --> 00:06:01,880
Mom said you're not supposed to gamble.

109
00:06:01,904 --> 00:06:02,947
Sleep, child!

110
00:06:03,447 --> 00:06:05,449
Mom? In here!

111
00:06:05,658 --> 00:06:07,658
I'll get those numbers to you tomorrow.

112
00:06:08,953 --> 00:06:11,163
Just tucking him in.

113
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:15,251
I got something for you.

114
00:06:16,752 --> 00:06:18,295
It's dirty.

115
00:06:19,171 --> 00:06:20,923
Well, that's 'cause it's the game ball.

116
00:06:21,131 --> 00:06:23,425
And you earned it, 'cause you helped us win.

117
00:06:24,468 --> 00:06:26,303
Okay, but can you wash it?

118
00:06:27,221 --> 00:06:29,890
Sheldon, your daddy's telling you he's proud of you.

119
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:32,893
I see. Thank you, dad.

120
00:06:33,811 --> 00:06:34,895
You're welcome.

121
00:06:37,648 --> 00:06:39,316
I'm still never touching that.

122
00:06:40,359 --> 00:06:41,443
Let's go wipe it off.

123
00:06:46,156 --> 00:06:52,788
- Adult For the next five weeks, I continued to help my father apply statistics to coach his team.

124
00:06:52,997 --> 00:06:58,252
Not surprisingly, they continued to win, which changed my status in the school dramatically.

125
00:06:58,460 --> 00:06:59,580
Yo, Sheldon! There he is!

126
00:07:00,838 --> 00:07:01,505
Shehdog!

127
00:07:01,714 --> 00:07:02,798
Math man!

128
00:07:03,549 --> 00:07:05,968
Hey, cutie.

129
00:07:06,719 --> 00:07:07,719
It was a nightmare.

130
00:07:07,887 --> 00:07:09,430
Shel-dog! Woo-hoo!

131
00:07:09,763 --> 00:07:12,516
Hugging, hair tousling, high fives.

132
00:07:12,725 --> 00:07:16,061
And as my popularity grew, so did my time aloft.

133
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:23,611
♪ everybody wants you.

134
00:07:32,578 --> 00:07:35,623
Hey, I've been looking all over for you.

135
00:07:36,248 --> 00:07:37,750
Do you know how popular we are?

136
00:07:38,292 --> 00:07:39,501
We? Yeah.

137
00:07:39,710 --> 00:07:42,171
I put the word out I was helping you with the football stats.

138
00:07:42,379 --> 00:07:43,881
And since I'm Asian, they bought it.

139
00:07:44,423 --> 00:07:46,133
Well, I'm glad you're enjoying it.

140
00:07:47,301 --> 00:07:48,010
You're not?

141
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:51,096
I was touched 82 times this afternoon.

142
00:07:51,305 --> 00:07:52,556
What do you mean, "touched"?

143
00:07:52,765 --> 00:07:54,141
Not inappropriately.

144
00:07:54,350 --> 00:07:55,434
Joyfully.

145
00:07:55,643 --> 00:07:57,061
Affectionately.

146
00:07:57,269 --> 00:07:59,438
A cheerleader hugged me to her bosom.

147
00:07:59,647 --> 00:08:00,856
That's amazing.

148
00:08:02,191 --> 00:08:03,400
No more high fives.

149
00:08:03,609 --> 00:08:05,235
I can't keep washing my hands.

150
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,117
Hey.

151
00:08:13,535 --> 00:08:15,371
There's my little assistant coach.

152
00:08:15,579 --> 00:08:16,914
Heho, dad.

153
00:08:18,248 --> 00:08:21,335
You have any more, uh, arithmetic ideas for next week's game?

154
00:08:21,543 --> 00:08:23,879
I do, but I'm trying to finish my homework.

155
00:08:25,589 --> 00:08:26,589
Ah.

156
00:08:29,176 --> 00:08:30,511
Looks complicated.

157
00:08:31,011 --> 00:08:33,180
Advanced chemistry. It's not.

158
00:08:34,223 --> 00:08:35,432
What are you guys doing?

159
00:08:35,891 --> 00:08:39,186
Your brother and I are gonna knock around a few ideas for the freeport game.

160
00:08:39,895 --> 00:08:40,895
Can I help?

161
00:08:41,146 --> 00:08:42,690
Actually, yeah. Run out to my truck.

162
00:08:42,898 --> 00:08:45,359
There's a little, uh, pocket calculator on my front seat.

163
00:08:45,651 --> 00:08:46,819
I got you a present.

164
00:08:47,653 --> 00:08:49,253
Thought it might help with your figuring.

165
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:51,699
I don't need a calculator, dad. I am one.

166
00:08:52,408 --> 00:08:53,033
Sure.

167
00:08:53,242 --> 00:08:54,242
Well...

168
00:08:54,994 --> 00:08:56,161
Go get it anyway.

169
00:08:57,871 --> 00:08:59,415
It's solar-powered.

170
00:08:59,873 --> 00:09:01,291
Can you imagine that?

171
00:09:20,144 --> 00:09:22,354
Georgie, turn that down!

172
00:09:22,563 --> 00:09:23,563
What?

173
00:09:28,068 --> 00:09:30,487
And look at this room. You need to clean this mess up.

174
00:09:30,696 --> 00:09:32,031
I'll get to it later.

175
00:09:32,239 --> 00:09:33,407
No, you'll get to it now.

176
00:09:33,615 --> 00:09:34,867
I don't feel like it.

177
00:09:35,284 --> 00:09:37,286
Well, your feelings have nothing to do with it.

178
00:09:37,494 --> 00:09:38,829
And stop throwing that ball.

179
00:09:39,038 --> 00:09:41,290
My room bothers you so much, you clean it.

180
00:09:43,625 --> 00:09:46,086
That's it! You are grounded! You hear me?!

181
00:09:46,295 --> 00:09:47,295
The hell?

182
00:09:49,590 --> 00:09:51,175
Hey...

183
00:09:51,383 --> 00:09:52,509
There's my little moonpie.

184
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:55,387
Did you get a chance to look at this week's games for me?

185
00:09:55,596 --> 00:09:58,724
Not yet. You understand there's a little time crunch involved.

186
00:09:58,932 --> 00:10:02,478
Meemaw's got some outstanding loans I need to pay back.

187
00:10:02,686 --> 00:10:06,398
I'm sorry, I have to finish my homework and then I have to help my dad.

188
00:10:08,275 --> 00:10:09,275
Come on.

189
00:10:09,693 --> 00:10:10,944
I'm your meemaw.

190
00:10:11,487 --> 00:10:12,613
I make you cookies.

191
00:10:12,821 --> 00:10:14,281
How 'bout a little quid pro quo?

192
00:10:14,490 --> 00:10:17,785
As much as I enjoy your use of Latin, no.

193
00:10:19,161 --> 00:10:20,621
Shelly, time to get ready for bed.

194
00:10:20,829 --> 00:10:21,997
But I'm not done.

195
00:10:22,206 --> 00:10:23,624
Don't you sass me, too, young man.

196
00:10:23,832 --> 00:10:25,167
Brush your teeth and get to bed.

197
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:32,633
I think your anger might be a little misdirected.

198
00:10:32,841 --> 00:10:34,134
Don't you start with me either.

199
00:10:34,593 --> 00:10:37,221
Now, see, you're still shootin' wide.

200
00:10:46,647 --> 00:10:48,065
Good evening, Mrs. Cooper.

201
00:10:48,273 --> 00:10:49,273
Can I speak to Sheldon?

202
00:10:49,399 --> 00:10:50,639
No, you can't speak to Sheldon.

203
00:10:50,734 --> 00:10:52,361
It's late. He's in bed.

204
00:10:52,569 --> 00:10:55,531
Oh. I was hoping he might like to go to a party with me.

205
00:10:55,739 --> 00:10:57,616
Has everyone lost their mind?

206
00:10:57,825 --> 00:10:59,409
He's a little boy, tam!

207
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:00,661
Good night!

208
00:11:02,037 --> 00:11:05,707
Good lord, that mouth of yours is a machine gun tonight.

209
00:11:11,797 --> 00:11:13,048
What are you doing?

210
00:11:13,382 --> 00:11:17,719
Trying to calculate the odds of the dolphins covering the spread next Sunday.

211
00:11:17,970 --> 00:11:18,970
I like dolphins.

212
00:11:19,012 --> 00:11:21,431
They talk out of that hole in their head.

213
00:11:23,809 --> 00:11:24,434
Hello.

214
00:11:24,643 --> 00:11:25,643
Tam?

215
00:11:29,314 --> 00:11:30,314
What are you doing here?

216
00:11:30,482 --> 00:11:32,109
Would you like to go to a party with me?

217
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:33,957
I don't want to go to a party with anyone.

218
00:11:33,986 --> 00:11:34,986
I would!

219
00:11:35,279 --> 00:11:35,904
Please, Sheldon.

220
00:11:36,113 --> 00:11:37,489
It's right across the street.

221
00:11:37,698 --> 00:11:39,533
Just get me in, and you can go back to bed.

222
00:11:39,950 --> 00:11:41,410
I have to ask my mom.

223
00:11:41,618 --> 00:11:43,412
No need. She knows all about the party.

224
00:11:45,372 --> 00:11:46,707
All right, then.

225
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,458
I need a minute to change.

226
00:11:52,671 --> 00:11:55,299
Why are you wearing that? It makes me look older.

227
00:11:56,592 --> 00:12:00,387
Just so we're clear, once you get in, I'm going home.

228
00:12:01,513 --> 00:12:02,806
Hey! Sheldon!

229
00:12:03,015 --> 00:12:04,183
What are you doing?

230
00:12:04,391 --> 00:12:06,991
Hey, everybody, check it out! Sheldon's here!

231
00:12:10,939 --> 00:12:13,108
I hope that doesn't wake up the kids.

232
00:12:13,317 --> 00:12:14,669
Should I go over there and say something?

233
00:12:14,693 --> 00:12:15,693
I think you should.

234
00:12:17,905 --> 00:12:18,906
I was bluffin'.

235
00:12:19,573 --> 00:12:21,241
Don't make me put my socks back on.

236
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:23,243
Never mind.

237
00:12:23,452 --> 00:12:24,661
Good night.

238
00:12:26,205 --> 00:12:27,289
Good night.

239
00:12:35,172 --> 00:12:37,049
I feel bad about yelling at Georgie.

240
00:12:38,091 --> 00:12:39,259
He deserved it.

241
00:12:39,635 --> 00:12:40,844
You should do it more.

242
00:12:41,136 --> 00:12:45,224
I think he's feeling left out now that you and Sheldon are spending so much time together.

243
00:12:48,685 --> 00:12:52,081
Are you kiddin' me? You're always saying to find something in common with Sheldon.

244
00:12:52,105 --> 00:12:54,125
And now that I have, you're telling me I'm ignoring Georgie?

245
00:12:54,149 --> 00:12:55,734
I'm not saying that.

246
00:12:55,943 --> 00:12:59,112
I'm just reminding you that you got two sons.

247
00:12:59,321 --> 00:13:00,530
I know.

248
00:13:02,199 --> 00:13:04,284
I also got a daughter I need to spend more time with.

249
00:13:04,493 --> 00:13:05,493
You do.

250
00:13:06,203 --> 00:13:07,443
But I wouldn't worry about her.

251
00:13:07,621 --> 00:13:08,997
She's an angel.

252
00:13:15,003 --> 00:13:16,838
- Yeah, Sheldon! Put me down!

253
00:13:17,047 --> 00:13:19,549
I said put me down!

254
00:13:19,758 --> 00:13:21,402
Put me down! I'm not enjoying this!

255
00:13:21,426 --> 00:13:23,095
Missy, what are you doing here?!

256
00:13:23,303 --> 00:13:25,097
Cuttin' loose. What are you doing here?

257
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:26,431
Slowly! Slowly!

258
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:27,683
Slowly!

259
00:13:29,101 --> 00:13:30,101
You, too?!

260
00:13:30,269 --> 00:13:31,603
Hello, Georgie!

261
00:13:31,812 --> 00:13:33,230
You're not supposed to be here.

262
00:13:33,438 --> 00:13:35,607
Neither are you! You're grounded!

263
00:13:37,025 --> 00:13:37,651
Come on.

264
00:13:37,859 --> 00:13:39,486
Both of you are going home. Now.

265
00:13:39,695 --> 00:13:41,863
Oh, thank goodness. Aw.

266
00:13:45,367 --> 00:13:46,535
How's puberty treating you?

267
00:13:46,743 --> 00:13:48,787
Because it is knocking me for a loop.

268
00:13:50,872 --> 00:13:51,872
Right?

269
00:13:58,505 --> 00:14:02,509
Somehow, my parents didn't find out about me partying heartily.

270
00:14:02,801 --> 00:14:06,596
But I did pay a price for burning the candle at both ends.

271
00:14:06,805 --> 00:14:09,224
Imade a mistake on a math test.

272
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:17,566
In my exhaustion, I did all the calculations in my head, and, like a common zoo animal, forgot to show my work.

273
00:14:18,775 --> 00:14:23,238
I just saw one of those girls from the party, and she acknowledged my existence by doing this.

274
00:14:24,281 --> 00:14:25,741
I've never felt so alive.

275
00:14:29,161 --> 00:14:30,161
Are you okay?

276
00:14:31,288 --> 00:14:32,288
No, I'm not.

277
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:35,709
Yeah, so?

278
00:14:36,626 --> 00:14:39,171
A b-plus... that's the beginning of the end.

279
00:14:39,588 --> 00:14:40,672
The end of what?

280
00:14:40,881 --> 00:14:41,923
My life.

281
00:14:42,132 --> 00:14:44,718
If I don't make some changes, who knows how far I'll fall.

282
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:48,221
I could wind up a drug addict, or a lawyer.

283
00:14:48,430 --> 00:14:50,140
Is it possible you're overreacting?

284
00:14:50,474 --> 00:14:54,269
No. Starting today, I'm done helping the football team.

285
00:14:54,561 --> 00:14:58,482
But if you do that, girls will no longer greet me like this.

286
00:14:59,441 --> 00:15:00,901
I'll greet you like that.

287
00:15:02,361 --> 00:15:03,904
It's not the same.

288
00:15:05,822 --> 00:15:09,951
Extricating myself from this situation was not going to be easy.

289
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:15,832
My father was counting on me, meemaw was counting on me, the school was counting on me.

290
00:15:16,124 --> 00:15:22,172
After much thought, I decided to employ the one strategic maneuver I knew I could count on.

291
00:15:22,464 --> 00:15:23,464
I tattled.

292
00:15:23,590 --> 00:15:24,590
Mom?

293
00:15:30,514 --> 00:15:36,186
j” robbin' people ♪ with a six-gun j” I fought the law ♪ and the law won...

294
00:15:36,395 --> 00:15:39,439
Sheldon got a b-plus! That's terrible for him!

295
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:42,442
I'm very disappointed in all three of you.

296
00:15:42,651 --> 00:15:45,404
That is right. Missy, this is for your ballet class.

297
00:15:45,612 --> 00:15:48,156
We do not go to parties.

298
00:15:48,448 --> 00:15:50,158
I am very disappointed.

299
00:15:56,123 --> 00:15:57,123
Hey.

300
00:15:58,333 --> 00:16:01,087
Got to go pick up some equipment for the team; You want to join me?

301
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:02,921
Can't. I'm grounded.

302
00:16:03,672 --> 00:16:05,340
Yeah, well...

303
00:16:05,590 --> 00:16:06,842
I won't tell if you won't.

304
00:16:09,678 --> 00:16:10,804
Sheldon going?

305
00:16:11,304 --> 00:16:13,098
That little snitch? Absolutely not.

306
00:16:19,271 --> 00:16:20,981
Sheldon still gonna help you with the math?

307
00:16:21,189 --> 00:16:22,482
I don't think so.

308
00:16:23,066 --> 00:16:25,152
But I did hear his little Asian friend can do it.

309
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:35,911
Hey.

310
00:16:36,371 --> 00:16:37,371
Hello.

311
00:16:37,706 --> 00:16:38,706
So...

312
00:16:39,124 --> 00:16:45,172
Oilers are a four-point favorite for this Sunday's game, but it's a home game, so I'm thinking I give the points.

313
00:16:46,047 --> 00:16:47,215
What do you think?

314
00:16:47,883 --> 00:16:49,968
I think I have to tell on you again.

315
00:16:50,177 --> 00:16:52,637
Go ahead. What's your mama gonna do, ground me?

316
00:16:56,766 --> 00:16:58,768
Take the oilers, give the points.

317
00:17:00,061 --> 00:17:03,064
I love you, moonpie.

318
00:17:06,526 --> 00:17:10,822
For the record, the oilers lost that game by four touchdowns.

319
00:17:11,239 --> 00:17:13,742
Meemaw never asked for my advice again.

320
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:20,790
Come on, come on, come on. Damn it!

321
00:17:21,041 --> 00:17:22,041
Okay.

322
00:17:22,834 --> 00:17:24,044
One more time.

323
00:17:25,462 --> 00:17:27,547
Mama needs a new jet ski!

324
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:28,839
And...

325
00:17:28,882 --> 00:17:30,091
Rat bastard!

326
00:17:32,427 --> 00:17:33,803
How you doin' there, Connie?

327
00:17:35,055 --> 00:17:36,932
Hey, Vincent.

328
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:38,725
What brings you to Louisiana?

329
00:17:38,934 --> 00:17:39,935
Wait, don't tell me.

330
00:17:40,143 --> 00:17:41,645
You're here to see Tony Orlando.

331
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:43,146
'Fraid not.

332
00:17:43,355 --> 00:17:44,795
Oh, well, you ought to check him out.

333
00:17:44,981 --> 00:17:47,192
He'll, uh, knock your socks off.

334
00:17:47,442 --> 00:17:48,902
I like my socks on.

335
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:52,864
Connie, you're putting me in a very awkward position.

336
00:17:54,157 --> 00:17:55,617
I won a toaster oven playing keno.

337
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:56,867
You want it?

338
00:17:58,328 --> 00:17:59,329
I got one.

339
00:18:00,205 --> 00:18:01,414
I want my money.

340
00:18:01,623 --> 00:18:03,166
All right.

341
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:04,668
Hang on.

342
00:18:06,753 --> 00:18:08,004
That's a very nice jacket.

343
00:18:08,213 --> 00:18:09,589
You're looking dapper.

344
00:18:13,552 --> 00:18:14,928
Ah.

345
00:18:15,387 --> 00:18:16,721
Hey, they comp my room here.

346
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:18,014
They do that for you?

347
00:18:18,348 --> 00:18:20,892
Actually, they frown upon my presence here.

348
00:18:21,101 --> 00:18:25,146
Oh. I also get a coupon for the breakfast buffet.

349
00:18:25,355 --> 00:18:26,523
You should look into that.

350
00:18:30,652 --> 00:18:31,652
Constance!

351
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:33,697
Patience, Vincenzo.

352
00:18:38,952 --> 00:18:40,620
Yes!

353
00:18:40,829 --> 00:18:42,372
Oh!

354
00:18:42,581 --> 00:18:44,499
All right, now we 're talking.

355
00:18:44,708 --> 00:18:46,710
Will you take a down payment in quarters?

356
00:18:46,918 --> 00:18:48,003
Do I have a choice?

357
00:18:49,546 --> 00:18:50,839
Start scoopin'.

358
00:18:51,256 --> 00:18:52,674
I got to go see Tony Orlando.

359
00:18:58,805 --> 00:18:59,806
Oof.

360
00:19:08,898 --> 00:19:09,898
Hey!

361
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:12,611
Hey, I need another cup!
